verdicts.what_would_resolve:
Count banded operations (SPD03 counters or Ir) for PC-lagged vs the banded direct RODAS5P on:
- the corpus semilinear 2-D family at n = 1536;
- one grid of at least 128x128;
- a problem that declares only its linear part.

Keep the candidate only where it wins.

verdicts.corrections:
Compare against three arms:
- the improved matrix-free arm, with orthogonalization counted;
- the banded or dense direct RODAS5P arm, in Ir;
- not the unimproved matrix-free arm.

Remove the 0.21x/0.68x merge figures. Fix the gate so it admits real-eigenvalue nonnormal operators, or drop the adv-diff row.

per_candidate.corrected_claim:
The candidate's JVP claims hold:
- closed-loop JVPs are 0.58-0.65x proj-stop;
- the retry arm gives a further 0.90x.

The cost claims do not:
- in admitted flops it is 2.8-5.8x more expensive than proj-stop;
- small-n figures are n+8 by construction, i.e. dense assembly;
- the budget-failure reduction is dominated by raising maxit.

per_candidate.next_probe:
Count JVPs, banded/sparse LU, solves and orthogonalization (or Ir) for this method against the SPD03 banded or sparse-direct RODAS5P, at matched error, on three problems:
- (i) the corpus semilinear 2-D family at n = 1536;
- (ii) a 2-D grid of at least 128x128 with sparse-LU fill;
- (iii) a problem that declares only its linear part.

PASS: total Ir <= 0.7x the direct arm on at least one of them.
KILL: it loses on all three.

Add ControllerKind::Predictive (cap optional) to adaptive.rs. Run a 17-point quarter-decade ladder on vdP, HIRES, Robertson and Bruss-50, plus Bruss-160 matrix-free.

Arms: I, I + uniform 0.725, PRED, PRED + cap. Use 3-4 h0 seeds. Score with both the regression frontier and the harness cheapest-run rule (median over seeds).

PASS requires all of:
- PRED <= 0.90 on vdP at >= 3 of 5 E under both rules;
- no problem > 1.06 (regression) or > 1.10 (cheapest-run);
- PRED beats I + uniform by >= 3% on HIRES or Bruss.

KILL on either:
- vdP >= 0.95 at every E;
- any problem > 1.08 on the regression frontier.

Noise arm: rerun with the INO targets and with relative eta 1e-4.

Replica only; this is cheap. Run a quarter-decade ladder over 1e-3 to 1e-8 with 4 h0 seeds on vdP, HIRES, Robertson, Bruss-50/200 and v2 rotating-nonnormal at n = 96.

Arms: GUS+cap, GUS+cap+gate, and GUS+cap with uniform safety in {0.85, 0.80, 0.75}. Score by the median over seeds under both matched-accuracy rules, with bootstrap confidence intervals.

Keep it only if all of these hold:
- it beats GUS+cap by >= 8% (geometric mean on vdP);
- it beats the best uniform-safety arm by >= 3%;
- it stays within +-4% elsewhere;
- it fires on <= 30% of steps on rotating-nonnormal.

Otherwise close it.

Freeze the threshold at 4 and freeze the validity guard. Then compute A_max on all 18 v2 n = 96 rows from the Rust dense arm, with both res5 and the exact step map, and report Ir overhead per driver.

KILL on any of:
- a row with true global / sum-of-true-local > 5 but A_max < 3;
- a non-amplifying row with A_max > 4 and no validity flag;
- res5 and the exact map disagreeing on the flag.

Build a switched replica (ROCK4 branch, shadow cost-per-unit-time trigger taken over from SOLVE-LIMITED-SWITCH, hysteresis). Run it on:
- the corpus v2 calibration families;
- Bruss-50/160/500;
- a 2-D real-spectrum problem without a declared band.

Compare at matched reference error against three arms: SPD07 matrix-free, the proj + INO matrix-free arm with orthogonalization counted, and SPD03 banded or dense direct in flops/Ir.

KILL if any of:
- it fires on no corpus family;
- it loses to the banded direct arm on every declared-structure case and has no undeclared-structure case;
- any silent instability occurs under rho_hat x 0.25;
- misroute overhead exceeds 1.25.

Admitting nonnormal operators requires an FOV step bound.
